From: GL-MT6000 fork <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] classify: feed the DSCP class selector to the egress TX queue selection

mqprio's traffic class map is not built from the DSCP.  The kernel indexes
dev->prio_tc_map with skb->priority & TC_BITMASK (netdevice.h) and
mtk_tx_hash() reads that map to choose the TX queues of a traffic class.
qosify only rewrites the DS field inside the IP header -- cake reads the
DSCP from the header -- so skb->priority stays 0 on forwarded traffic and
every packet ends up in the class held by prio_tc_map[0].

Set skb->priority to the DSCP class selector (the three high bits, giving
CS0..CS7) once the DS field has been written, on the egress path only.  The
egress filter runs before ndo_select_queue(), so the value is visible to
mtk_tx_hash() when the upload leaves the WAN port.

Signed-off-by: GL-MT6000 fork <noreply@localhost>
---
 qosify-bpf.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/qosify-bpf.c b/qosify-bpf.c
--- a/qosify-bpf.c
+++ b/qosify-bpf.c
@@ -549,6 +549,13 @@
 	else
 		dscp = ipv6_get_dscp(skb, iph_offset);

+	/* Feed the DSCP class selector to the egress TX queue selection:
+	 * mqprio's prio_tc_map is indexed by skb->priority & TC_BITMASK and
+	 * mtk_tx_hash() reads it to pick the traffic class queue.
+	 */
+	if (!ingress)
+		skb->priority = dscp >> 3;
+
 	account_dscp(dscp, packets, skb->len);

 	return TC_ACT_UNSPEC;
